                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/\Gamma \to E
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              which map every morphism of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/\Gamma
              to a cartesian arrow. Type-theoretically, we can think of such an object as a type together with
              %em specified
              compatible substitutions along any possible morphism. That type-formers may be extended in this case was proven by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Hofmann"} Martin Hofmann
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sums"} dependent sums
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+products"} dependent products
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+type+theory"} extensional type theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intensional+type+theory"} intensional type theory
              (particularly not their
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term+elimination"} eliminator
            %p
              A different construction (due to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Power"} John Power
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E'
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma\in C
              to consist of a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:\Gamma \to \Delta
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              along with an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,A)
              as a type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              with a “delayed substitution”
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %a{:href => "#LumsdaineWarren13"} Lumsdaine &amp; Warren (2015)
              that essentially all type formers can be extended to it from
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %h3#universes Universes
          %p
            Suppose given a particular morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mover
                    %mi U
                    %mo ˜
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:\widetilde{U} \to U
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryWithAttributes"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\to C
            corresponds to the representable presheaf
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(-,U)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\to C^I
            is defined by pullback of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            as a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe"}> universe
            ” of types. We may then of course pass to a contextual category, via example
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FromComprehensionToContextual"}
          %p
            Type-forming operations may be extended strictly in this case by performing them once in the “universal” case, then acting by composition. This construction is due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Voevodsky"} Voevodsky
            = succeed "\u2013" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+types"} type of types
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
          %p Particular important universes include:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+universe"} Grothendieck universe
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe+in+a+topos"} universe in a topos
                = succeed "-small" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %li
              %p
                In the category
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gpd"} Gpd
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+opfibrations"} split opfibrations
                with small fibers. Similarly, we can consider the groupoid of small sets, whose display maps are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+opfibrations"} discrete opfibrations
                with small fibers.
            %li
              %p
                In the category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+Kan+fibration"} universal Kan fibration
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mover
                        %mi U
                        %mo ˜
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:\widetilde{U} \to U
                which classifies all
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrations"} Kan fibrations
                with small fibers.
          %h3#simple_fibrations Simple fibrations
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be any category with finite products, and define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\to C
            to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+fibration"} discrete fibration
            corresponding to the presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}\to Set
            which is constant at
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ob(C)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            are pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Gamma,A)
            of objects of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Gamma,A) \to (\Delta,A)
            induced by a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma\to\Delta
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Define the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\to C^I
            to take
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Gamma,A)
            to the projection
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma\times A \to \Gamma
            %em simple fibration
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            The dependent type theory which results from this structure “has no nontrivial dependency”. That is, whenever we have a dependent type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash (A \;type)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a type in the empty context (that is, we have
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vdash (A\; type)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            %em simple
            (non-dependent) type theory — hence the name “simple fibration”.
          %h3#the_big_model_of_locally_cartesian_closed_categories The big model of locally cartesian closed categories
          #BigModelLocallyCartesianClosed.num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p
              Ignoring coherence issues, the CwF induced by a locally cartesian closed (lcc) category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TypeTheoryModelFromLocallyCartesianClosedCategory"}
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                  %th
                    In
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  %th
                    In terms of slices of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  %th Big model
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Contexts
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    Objects
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \in \mathcal{C}
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    Slice categories
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi Γ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{/ \Gamma}
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    Lcc categories
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Context Morphisms
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    Morphisms
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo :
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo →
                          %mi Δ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : \Gamma \rightarrow \Delta
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    Lcc functors
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                          %mo :
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi Δ
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi Γ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* : \mathcal{C}_{/ \Delta} \rightarrow \mathcal{C}_{/ \Gamma}
                    over
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    Lcc functors
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo :
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo →
                          %mi Γ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : \Delta \rightarrow \Gamma
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Types
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    Morphisms
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                          %mo :
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} dom
                          %mi σ
                          %mo →
                          %mi Γ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma : \operatorname{dom} \sigma \rightarrow \Gamma
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    Objects
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi Γ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \in \mathcal{C}_{/ \Gamma}
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    Objects
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi Γ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \in \Gamma
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Terms
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    Sections
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo :
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⇆
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} dom
                          %mi σ
                          %mo :
                          %mi σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s : \Gamma \leftrightarrows \operatorname{dom} \sigma : \sigma
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    Morphisms
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo :
                          %msub
